	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Silithus is a wasteland of yellow sand and broken stone in the far south-west of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, beyond the western rim of {link:un-goro-crater}Un'Goro Crater{/link}. Nothing green grows here willingly. Great hives of the silithid rise from the desert like swollen towers, and the wind carries a dry humming that never quite stops. In the south-west, a wall of dark stone shuts away an ancient city. The {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} remember this land as the field of their bitterest war. They sealed its enemy away long ago. Now the sands are shifting again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records who first walked these sands. The oldest histories speak of the {link:qiraji}Qiraji{/link}, an insect people who raised the fortress of Ahn'Qiraj in the south and ruled the silithid swarms from within its walls. Nearly a thousand years ago, the Qiraji marched out of the desert to conquer {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. The night elves met them here under {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link}, and lost. The whole desert fell, and the night elves were driven east to the edge of {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link}. Only when the dragonflights joined them was the swarm stopped. Together they walled it up inside its own city. That struggle is remembered as the {link:war-of-the-shifting-sands}War of the Shifting Sands{/link}. The ruins of the night elves' outposts still lie in the desert, and their dead do not rest easily.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link} has returned to Silithus. Its druids and soldiers hold {link:cenarion-hold}Cenarion Hold{/link} in the heart of the desert, and its emissaries call on the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} alike to come and fight the silithid before the swarm spreads. The three great hives, {link:hive-ashi}Hive'Ashi{/link}, {link:hive-zora}Hive'Zora{/link} and {link:hive-regal}Hive'Regal{/link}, grow busier by the day. Strange glyphed crystals stand within them, and the Circle's scholars believe that something sends orders to the swarm through them.

The silithid are not the only threat. The {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} has built camps across the west of the desert, where its cultists raise wind stones and call up the nobles of an elemental council. At {link:bronzebeard-encampment}Bronzebeard Encampment{/link} in the south, dwarves of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} search the hives for lost relics; their leader, {link:brann-bronzebeard}Brann Bronzebeard{/link}, has gone missing again. The commander of Cenarion Hold has lost his wife to the hives. The dwarves swear they have seen dragons in the sky, where no dragon has flown for a thousand years. Beyond the {link:the-scarab-wall}Scarab Wall{/link}, the {link:qiraji}Qiraji{/link} wait.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link}.{/b} Druids, scholars and soldiers of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} and the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, who hold {link:cenarion-hold}Cenarion Hold{/link} and keep watch at {link:valor-s-rest}Valor's Rest{/link}.
• {b}The silithid.{/b} Stingers, drones, reavers, tunnelers and wasps of the three hives, and the overlords who rule them.
• {b}The {link:qiraji}Qiraji{/link}.{/b} The masters of the swarm, sealed behind the {link:the-scarab-wall}Scarab Wall{/link} in the city of Ahn'Qiraj.
• {b}The {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link}.{/b} Cultists, geolords, keepers and prophets in camps across the western desert, and in a cave called {link:twilight-s-run}Twilight's Run{/link}.
• {b}The elementals.{/b} Desert rumblers, dust stormers and cyclone warriors, and the templars of the {link:abyssal-council}Abyssal Council{/link}.
• {b}The dwarves.{/b} Delvers of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} at {link:bronzebeard-encampment}Bronzebeard Encampment{/link}.
• {b}The beasts.{/b} Stonelash scorpids, sand skitterers, rock stalkers and great dredge worms that prey on the caravans.
• {b}The dead.{/b} The tortured spirits of the druids and sentinels who fell at {link:southwind-village}Southwind Village{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Age of the Hives.{/b} Long before the night elves came, the {link:qiraji}Qiraji{/link} raised Ahn'Qiraj and bred their swarms beneath the sand.
• {b}The {link:war-of-the-shifting-sands}War of the Shifting Sands{/link}.{/b} The Qiraji invaded {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. {link:southwind-village}Southwind Village{/link} fell, and with it {link:valstann-staghelm}Valstann Staghelm{/link}. The night elves were driven back to {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link}, until the dragonflights joined the fight and helped seal Ahn'Qiraj behind a great barrier.
• {b}The Long Silence.{/b} For centuries the wall held. The desert was left to the silithid and the dead.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link} has come back, the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} has come with its own purposes, and the hives are stirring.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Sands",
			text = [=[• The innkeeper of {link:cenarion-hold}Cenarion Hold{/link} learned to cook sandworm from a cookbook found in a {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} camp. She admits that the dumplings are better than she expected from such people.
• The dwarves of {link:bronzebeard-encampment}Bronzebeard Encampment{/link} claim that among them, counting the monkey, they know thirty-eight languages. None of them could name the tongue that {link:natalia-mar-alith}Natalia Mar'alith{/link} chanted in.
• A watcher in the eastern desert says he has been slain a hundred times, and that he always wakes again in the same place.
• The Twilight's Hammer circulates a monthly bulletin among its faithful, written in a cipher. Its deserters read it too.]=],
		},
	},
})

